# CPO Retail Command Center — Mercedes-Benz Framing

The Streamlit demo now wraps the pricing model inside a full **CPO Retail Command Center**: a National Executive Overview, separate Sales and After-sales KPI systems, a 50-dealer Dealer 360 with a composite Dealer Score, and the CPO pricing & inventory action layer. This section is for explaining *why* it is designed that way, grounded in dealer-analytics experience.

> Compliance note: the dealer network is 100% synthetic. Use no real Mercedes-Benz data, dealer names, customers, VINs, targets, or incentive values in any interview. Frame everything as "this is how I would design it, based on the kind of dealer analytics I worked on."

## "What I did → so I designed it this way" (English)

- **I built KPI dashboards for 50+ dealers nationally**, so the demo opens with an Executive Overview of the 10 metrics management watches first — five Sales, five After-sales — with monthly trends and an alert that surfaces the one dealer slipping in the ranking.
- **I ran Sales and After-sales operating analysis**, so I split them into two separate KPI systems. Sales tracks NC, CPO, and Vans achievement *separately* — different targets, mix, and inventory logic mean you never sum them before comparing. After-sales only shows metrics that can change a dealer's action: absorption, workshop utilization, technician efficiency, retention, first-time fix, CSI.
- **I worked on pricing and inventory analysis**, so the used-car ML model becomes the action layer: it scores each CPO vehicle, and aged or overpriced stock turns into reprice / promote / transfer recommendations with a 30-day sell-probability and margin-at-risk view.
- **I cared about overall dealer health**, so I designed a transparent Dealer Score — 45% Sales, 35% After-sales, 15% Customer Experience, 5% Compliance — that ranks dealers but always lets you drill into the raw KPIs to see *why* a dealer dropped.

## "我在奔驰做过什么 → 所以这样设计" (中文)

- **做过全国 50+ 经销商 KPI 看板** → demo 首屏就是全国总览,放管理层最先看的 10 个指标(5 个 Sales、5 个 After-sales),加月度趋势和"某经销商排名下滑"的预警。
- **做过 Sales 与 After-sales 经营分析** → 把两者拆成各自的 KPI 体系。Sales 把 NC / CPO / Vans 的目标达成率*分别*计算 —— 目标、车型结构、库存逻辑都不同,不能相加后比较。After-sales 只放能改变门店动作的指标:吸收率、工位利用率、技师效率、回厂率、一次修复率、满意度。
- **做过定价与库存分析** → 二手车 ML 模型成为行动层:为每辆 CPO 车打分,把老化、定价偏高的库存转化为调价 / 促销 / 跨店调拨建议,并给出 30 天售出概率和风险毛利。
- **关注经销商综合健康度** → 设计了透明的 Dealer Score(45% Sales + 35% After-sales + 15% 客户体验 + 5% 合规),用于排名,但始终能下钻到原始 KPI,解释经销商*为什么*掉队。

## The Demo Storyline (90 seconds)

"National sales achievement looks healthy — about 100%. But on the Executive Overview, an alert shows dealer **MB-E07** has dropped to the bottom of the 50-dealer ranking. I drill in: NC sales are fine, but **CPO achievement is only 78%**, days-supply and 90-plus-day aging are high. On the After-sales tab the same dealer trails on **retention (61%) and CSI**. Dealer 360 confirms the root cause with the composite score and a radar of the four indices. Finally the CPO tab shows **29 E-Class units stuck 90-plus days, overpriced versus the model's fair value** — so the action list recommends repricing those first, promoting the rest, and transferring slow movers, plus a service package to win back retention. That's the whole loop: national monitoring → dealer diagnosis → single-car pricing action."

