## Anticipated Questions

- **"Is this real Mercedes data?"** No. Everything in the dealer network is synthetic and deterministic. I designed the metric system and decision flow from the kind of dealer analytics I worked on; the numbers, names, and formulas are transparent portfolio assumptions, not company definitions.
- **"Why a composite Dealer Score instead of raw KPIs?"** The score is for ranking and triage across 50 dealers; the raw indices and KPI drill-down are always one click away so the score never hides the cause.
- **"Why is Service Absorption flagged?"** It needs a credible fixed-operating-cost field. It is synthetic here; in a real deployment I would only show it once that expense data is trustworthy, rather than fabricating a number for the sake of looking complete.
